  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for NRS_484B_223_4b (6 witnesses), using 3 of the 6 runs.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_223_4b.lean`):\n- **Subject class:** `ru_aggregate subject \"DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle\"`.\n- **When it applies:** at the moment the subject leaves an intersection `x`. At that moment there must be a turn lane `l` whose side is right and which enters `x`. The subject's footprint must also have overlapped `l` at some observation from its latest entry into `x` up to that exit. The latest entry cuts off any earlier overlap, so only the current passage counts.\n- **Duty:** at that exit, `drv_motion_right_turn_through_region(subject, x)` must have just become true, using the three reading parameters. The duty applies to every intersection that meets the conditions above.\n- **No narrowings of my own.**\n\n**What failed before the pass:**\n1. **Run 1:** the `permit` witness kept a fixed heading while its yaw rate said it was turning, and the gate rejected the trace.\n2. **Run 2:** I removed the heading. The gate then rejected the trace because, with occupancy observed, a track needs a heading to have a footprint.\n3. **Run 3 (OK):** I rebuilt the right turn as two exact 45° steps (north, then north-east, then east). That gives a total change of −90° since entry. I also made every witness's stated occupancy match its actual footprint geometry.\n\n**Two things worth knowing:**\n- **Window:** every witness only counts instants from 50 ms on. At the first scene, the \"subject just left the intersection\" test has no previous observation, so it is unknown there.\n- **`occasion_s3` differs slightly from its narrative.** The narrative says the subject is in the intersection only after its entry. In the built scene its rear stays in the plain through lane until it clears the approach, because a 4 m car can't leave the approach lanes in one 50 ms step. It never touches the right turn lane after entry, which is what that scenario tests.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory. No dependency defect was found.",
